---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy"
  description="How Kitfy handles your files, the one AI exception, analytics, and ads."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-(--container-content) px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">Privacy</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-6 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-fg-secondary">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">Your files</h2>
        <p>
          The tools process files inside your browser using JavaScript running on your own device. Files are not
          uploaded, not stored, and not seen by anyone. Closing the tab is enough to remove everything.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">The one exception</h2>
        <p>
          Sprout's meal photo feature sends the image to an AI service to estimate calories. That is stated on the
          page before you use it. No other tool sends anything anywhere.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Page views are counted so it is possible to tell which tools are worth maintaining. This records the
          page, the country, and the kind of device. It does not record who you are.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">Ads</h2>
        <p>
          Google AdSense serves the ads and may set cookies to decide what to show you. Google's own
          <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="text-fg underline underline-offset-4"
          >
            policy
          </a> governs that, and it is linked at the bottom of this page.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-6 text-xl font-display font-bold tracking-(--tracking-display) text-fg">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you want anything about your usage removed, the
          <a href="mailto:hello@kitfy.work" class="text-fg underline underline-offset-4">footer contact link</a>
          is the way to ask.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
